   0.8431372549019608],ExpressionUUID->"60c5a955-a6bb-1c46-b180-cd8b250af911"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["The program contained in this notebook works well \
when the object is at finite distance from the first surface of the optical \
system.\n\nThis program has the following input  :\nrad = list of radii\n\
thick = list of distances between the  surfaces \nind = the refractive \
between the surfaces\ncostasf = aspheric constants of dioptrics\nstoprad = \
radius of the stop\nnstop = number of the dioptrics before the stop\ndis = \
distance of the stop from the last dioptric before the stop\ndobject = \
distance of the object from the first dioptric\nhobject = height of the \
object from the optical axis\nwaves = wave length\norder=3 or 5 if we are \
interested in the third or third+fifth order aberrations.\n\nOften \
astigmatism and distorsion have very small values. In these cases it is \
important the order of magnitude.\n",
 FontSize->16]], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.45519372409375*^9, 3.455193838375*^9}, {
  3.455194346921875*^9, 3.455194379125*^9}, {3.456019290990428*^9, 
  3.456019335443553*^9}, {3.9688292916612854`*^9, 3.968829868279871*^9}, {
  3.968832024776001*^9, 3.968832041022328*^9}, {3.9698379160546017`*^9, 
  3.969838020058758*^9}, {3.9698380684816685`*^9, 3.9698383541329*^9}, {
